6. Full Claim Lifecycle Specification
6.1 Claim Lifecycle Schema
The claim lifecycle schema defines the structure of a claim lifecycle deposit.

It has the following fields:

lifecycle_id. A string. Required.

claim_id. A string. Required.

claim_description. A string. Required.

source_app. An enum. Required. The values are physics_knowledge_library, replication_tracker, anomaly_register, medical_claim_verifier, psychological_effect_registry, climate_attribution_registry, historical_claim_registry, mathematical_conjecture_registry, legal_precedent_graph, economic_indicator_provenance, other.

current_status. An enum. Required. The values are proposed, tested, replicated, contested, superseded, withdrawn, other.

current_confidence. An enum. Required. The values are very_high, high, medium, low, very_low, unknown.

trajectory. An enum. Required. The values are toward_acceptance, toward_rejection, stable, oscillating, unclear.

lifecycle_events. An array of lifecycle event objects. Required.

key_events. An array of key event objects. Optional.

relations. An array of claim relation objects. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each lifecycle event object has:

event_id. A string.

event_date. A string in ISO8601 format.

previous_status. An enum. The values are proposed, tested, replicated, contested, superseded, withdrawn, other.

new_status. An enum. The values are proposed, tested, replicated, contested, superseded, withdrawn, other.

event_reason. A string.

event_drivers. An array of driver objects.

event_actors. An array of actor objects.

event_evidence. An array of evidence objects.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each driver object has:

driver_id. A string.

driver_description. A string.

driver_type. An enum. The values are new_evidence, new_study, replication_result, methodological_critique, theoretical_advance, retraction, community_consensus, other.

Each actor object has:

actor_id. A string.

actor_name. A string.

actor_type. An enum. The values are individual_researcher, research_group, journal, institution, community, automated_system, other.

actor_role. An enum. The values are proponent, opponent, neutral_arbiter, observer, other.

Each evidence object has:

evidence_id. A string.

evidence_description. A string.

evidence_reference. A string.

evidence_type. An enum. The values are study, meta_analysis, replication, data, argument, other.

Each key event object has:

key_event_id. A string.

key_event_date. A string in ISO8601 format.

key_event_description. A string.

key_event_significance. An enum. The values are major, moderate, minor.

Each claim relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_claim_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are depends_on, alternative, supersedes, superseded_by, supports, contradicts, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

